5e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [24]}], "matchEvidence": "Reviewed patient cases and question topics in the exact-recording transcript against the printed task paper; task filename alone is not used"}, {"id": "british-academy-task-2-B", "label": "British Academy · Task 2 · Part B", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "pages": [16, 17, 18], "questions": [{"number": 25, "prompt": "You hear a monologue by a physician explaining to his staff about\nCutaneous manifestations.\n\nWhich of the following is a cutaneous sign of vomiting?\n\nA. Telogen effluvium\n\nB. Knuckle calluses\n\nC. Xerosis", "sourcePage": 16, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 26, "prompt": "You hear a monologue by a physician explaining to his staff about\nsymptoms of anorexia nervosa.\n\nWhich of the following statements is incorrect?\n\nA. Mitral valve prolapse can cause chest pain.\n\n\n\nB. Abnormal ejection fraction was seen in most patients with anorexia nervosa\n\nC. Long standing hypovolemia causes chest palpitations", "sourcePage": 16, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 27, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a physician and his nurse about\nendometriosis\n\nEndometriosis is;\n\nA. Endometrial tissue formed inside the uterine cavity\n\nB. Broken endometrial tissue\n\nC. Displaced endometrial tissue", "sourcePage": 17, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 28, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a physician and his nurse about the\ntreatments for the signs of eating disorders.\n\nTopical tocopherol is effective in the treatment of\n\nA. Xerosis\n\nB. Acne\n\nC. Angular stomatitis", "sourcePage": 17, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 29, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a physician and his junior about pain\ntransmission.\n\nNon-nociceptive signals are carried by the;\n\nA. Large nerve fibers\n\nB. Small nerve fibers\n\nC. Projection neuron", "sourcePage": 18, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 30, "prompt": "You hear a discussion between a physician his nurse about subclinical\nseizures.\n\nWhich of the following statements is incorrect?\n\nA. Unusual electrical activity in the brain causes a subclinical seizure.\n\nB. Electroencephalogram is a treatment method for autism.\n\nC. Signs such as aggression or meltdowns were seen in the autistic patient.\n\n                                      PART C\n\nIn this part of the test, you'll hear two different extracts. In each\nextract, you'll hear health professionals talking about specific aspects\nof their work.\n\nFor questions 31 to 42 choose the answer (A, B, or C) which fits best\naccording to what you hear. Complete the answers as you listen the\naudio.\n\nNow, look at extract one.", "sourcePage": 18, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["7b30a4b5460c8e74c80de610ca75982a1990a6f00ec019fe0f82c66d38e580f1"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [24]}], "matchEvidence": "Reviewed patient cases and question topics in the exact-recording transcript against the printed task paper; task filename alone is not used"}, {"id": "british-academy-task-2-C", "label": "British Academy · Task 2 · Part C", "part": "C", "sourceSha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "pages": [19, 20, 21, 22, 23], "questions": [{"number": 31, "prompt": "Colon and rectal cancer screening is suggested to;\n\nA. The people up to the age of 75, if maintaining good health.\n\nB. The people up to the age of 85, if maintaining good health.\n\nC. People above 85, if maintaining good health.", "sourcePage": 19, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 32, "prompt": "Pap screening is suggested once in every 3 years for the age group;\n\nA. 30 to 65\n\nB. 21 to 29\n\n\n\nC. Above 65", "sourcePage": 19, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 33, "prompt": "A Pap test in addition to HPV test is recommended for;\n\nA. The women above 65 years\n\nB. The women between 30 and 65\n\nC. The women who had a total hysterectomy", "sourcePage": 20, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 34, "prompt": "Mammograms once every two years is recommended for the age group;\n\nA. 40 to 44\n\nB. Above 55\n\nC. 45 to 54", "sourcePage": 20, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 35, "prompt": "For yearly screening of lung cancer, the person\n\nA. Should not have smoked 30 pack per year for 15 years\n\nB. Should have a smoking history of a maximum of 30 pack per year\n\nC. Should have a smoking history of a minimum of 30 pack per year", "sourcePage": 20, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 36, "prompt": "Which of the following statements is incorrect;\n\nA. Research hasn’t proven yet that the risk factors outweigh the benefits of\nscreening\n\nB. One should get a prostate specific antigen blood test prior to the screening\n\nC. Men should not get screened for prostate cancer without knowing the risk\nfactors", "sourcePage": 21, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 37, "prompt": "Which of the following statements is incorrect?\n\nA. Gut-brain communication will decrease memory and learning abilities.\n\nB. Gut has a strong communication with brain\n\nC. Gut is considered as the second brain", "sourcePage": 21, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 38, "prompt": "A long nerve called vagus nerve\n\nA. Lies inside the gastrointestinal tract.\n\nB. Lies inside the brain\n\nC. Controls our digestive system", "sourcePage": 22, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 39, "prompt": "Feeding behavior is initiated by;\n\nA. The signals from the gastrointestinal tract.\n\nB. hippocampal activity\n\nC. vagal nerve stimulation", "sourcePage": 22, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 40, "prompt": "Signals to stop eating is transmitted from\n\nA. Brain to gut\n\nB. Gut to brain\n\nC. From hippocampus to gastrointestinal tract", "sourcePage": 22, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "B", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 41, "prompt": "When the gut-brain pathway was detached;\n\nA. The rats could effectively access spatial memories provoked by the\ngastrointestinal system\n\nB. The rats could still access the food with their spatial memory\n\nC. The rats could access the food with the help of activated vagus nerve", "sourcePage": 23, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "C", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}, {"number": 42, "prompt": "What is the conclusion of this research?\n\nA. Disruption of the vagal nerve does not affect social learning, body weight or\nanxiety.\n\nB. Endogenous connection from gut to the hippocampus mediates the cognitive\npathway.\n\nC. vBLOC therapy, has been effective in weight loss by electrically disrupting the\nvagus nerve.", "sourcePage": 23, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "answer": {"text": "A", "page": 24, "source": {"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper"}}}], "skills": ["listening"], "recordings": ["7b30a4b5460c8e74c80de610ca75982a1990a6f00ec019fe0f82c66d38e580f1"], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-0300375e981d9b16a421", "filename": "Listening Tests 1 - 15.pdf", "sha256": "0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-3/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/0300375e981d9b16a4214982bdc40c52b4b76d2e6197811448bc8dcb96f2f8fc.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "paper", "pages": [24]}], "matchEvidence": "Reviewed patient cases and question topics in the exact-recording transcript against the printed task paper; task filename alone is not used"}]}
